window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["23"]={"https://theconversation.com/nepal-tibet-floods-showed-the-need-for-greater-climate-finance-is-the-world-listening-294675":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"6b582fa89b46f6a36bce625b0b1518184ec067af6f65cb7973033f4778797fcf","read":"https://theconversation.com/nepal-tibet-floods-showed-the-need-for-greater-climate-finance-is-the-world-listening-294675","bytes":184513,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Nepal-Tibet floods showed the need for greater climate finance. Is the world listening?","by":[{"n":"Melanie Pill","r":"Honorary Senior Lecturer, Australian National University"}],"pub":"2026-11-11T17:29:31Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Earlier this year, a ",["massive flash flood","https://theconversation.com/nepals-flash-floods-show-the-devastating-power-of-cascading-hazards-290611"]," ripped through Nepalese and Tibetan townships along the Bhote Koshi river system, leaving more than 1,400 people dead and at least 5,000 missing."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Climate change contributed","https://theconversation.com/nepal-tibet-disaster-linked-to-climate-change-a-glaciologist-explains-290656"]," to the glacial mountain collapse that triggered the floods. But Nepal, a developing country of about 30 million people, only produces 0.05% of the world’s carbon emissions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Left with a ",["multi-billion dollar reconstruction bill","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-09-12/nepal-flood-reconstruction-cost-billions/107145518"],", Nepal is a clear-cut example of the need for greater climate finance – the funding to help developing countries protect their people and economies against climate disasters, and rebuild when they happen."]},{"k":"p","s":["But time and time again, ",["United Nations climate summits fall short","https://www.ituc-csi.org/COP29-Talks-end-with-utterly-inadequate-deal"]," of agreements that would provide enough climate finance to match the magnitude of climate change. Will COP31 be any different?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Climate disasters will send many countries into a debt spiral – but there’s a way out","https://theconversation.com/climate-disasters-will-send-many-countries-into-a-debt-spiral-but-theres-a-way-out-269318"]]},{"k":"h","s":["What is climate finance?"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Climate finance","https://unfccc.int/topics/introduction-to-climate-finance"]," is the funding that helps countries protect their people and economies from the damage wrought by global warming. It includes projects like building sea walls to protect from floods and sea-level rise, developing drought-tolerant crops or enhancing infrastructure so buildings and transport networks can withstand extreme weather. Climate finance can also fund investments that mitigate – or reduce – carbon emissions, such as renewable energy and electric transport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Since climate diplomacy began in 1995 with the first UN climate summit, developing countries – particularly ",["in the Pacific","https://theconversation.com/ahead-of-the-global-climate-summit-pacific-leaders-call-on-nations-to-keep-1-5-c-within-reach-292766"]," – have fought for greater availability of climate finance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Their argument ",["is this","https://theconversation.com/cop29-who-pays-for-climate-action-in-developing-nations-and-how-much-becomes-more-urgent-242678"],": wealthy countries should lead on climate finance because they developed with the benefit of fossil fuels, and contribute the most to climate change. In comparison, developing countries have limited resources, and emit negligible amounts of greenhouse gases but suffer disproportionate climate consequences."]},{"k":"p","s":["At the 2024 climate summit in Baku, Azerbaijan, a ",["new finance agreement","https://theconversation.com/cop29-climate-finance-deal-why-poor-countries-are-so-angry-244341"]," was reached. Developed countries committed to raise US$300 billion (A$436 billion) a year for the world’s poorest nations by 2035. This might sound ambitious, but it is nowhere near enough to address the global need."]},{"k":"p","s":["At the recent pre-COP31 talks in Fiji, Pacific leaders made it ",["abundantly clear","https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20261007-australia-touts-new-funds-for-pacific-infrastructure-at-fiji-pre-cop"]," climate finance was crucial for the survival of vulnerable countries."]},{"k":"h","s":["What is climate ‘loss and damage’?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Developing countries, such as those in the Himalayas as well as small island nations, are ",["particularly vulnerable","https://www.oecd.org/en/publications/2025/11/the-climate-action-monitor-2025_aed0c4bb/full-report/how-vulnerable-are-countries-to-climate-risks_92df65fe.html"]," to climate change because of their geographic exposure, reliance on sectors such as agriculture and lower capacity to adapt. The concept of “loss and damage” reflects the unavoidable and irreversible harm from climate change."]},{"k":"p","s":["The push to secure an official UN-backed loss and damage fund was a contentious and decades-long process, fraught with resistance from wealthy nations. So developing nations were jubilant at the close of COP27 in Eygpt in 2022, when wealthy countries finally agreed to establish a fund to respond to loss and damage."]},{"k":"p","s":["This fund made its first call for submissions at COP30 in Belém in 2025, and received almost 180 requests totalling US$2.8 billion (A$4 billion) by the June 2026 deadline. While pledges to the fund now exceed US$820 million (A$1.2 billion), there is a ",["significant financing gap","https://www.frld.org/sites/default/files/Press%20Release_Post%20B.9%20communique.pdf"]," compared to the demand."]},{"k":"p","s":["What exactly this fund will pay for, and how, is unclear. However, the catastrophe on the Nepal-Tibet border served as the first litmus test. Nepal made an urgent appeal to the fund and asked for an emergency payout of the maximum allowable amount of US$20 million (A$29 million)."]},{"k":"p","s":["At its first ever extraordinary meeting, the fund’s board decided to set aside ",["US$21.6 million","https://www.frld.org/sites/default/files/FRLD_Press_Release_Nepal_22Oct2026-2.pdf"]," (A$31 million). This is only about ",["0.7% of Nepal’s","https://www.carbonbrief.org/analysis-nepals-20m-loss-and-damage-claim-only-covers-0-7-of-flood-costs"]," actual economic loss and damage cost. And it doesn’t include non-economic losses related to health, culture or nature."]},{"k":"p","s":["The speed of that decision is historic in the notoriously snail-paced UN process. Other countries will have to wait until December 2026 for ",["the outcome of their submissions","https://www.frld.org/sites/default/files/FRLD_Press_Release_Nepal_22Oct2026-2.pdf"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["How Australia should act"]},{"k":"p","s":["As the president of COP31 negotiations, Australia’s climate minister Chris Bowen has an opportunity to elevate the topics that Turkey is strategically avoiding. These include the need for a fossil fuel phase-out – only by reducing greenhouse gas emissions can disasters such as the one in Nepal be prevented. Australia must also be an ally to island nations across the Pacific."]},{"k":"p","s":["In terms of finance, Australia should rally more support for the ",["Pacific Resilience Facility","https://forumsec.org/pacific-resilience-facility"],". This Pacific-owned and led fund acts as a self-sustaining financial model. It relied on an ",["endowment fund structure","https://forumsec.org/pacific-resilience-facility"]," designed to generate predictable, continuous returns, eliminating the need for repeating donation cycles or accumulating national debt. This fund aims to directly benefit communities on the ground, including addressing loss and damage. But it requires more long-term investment."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ultimately, no amount of finance can respond to the damage that climate change is already causing across the globe. It is absolutely vital that COP31 genuinely focuses on eliminating its root cause: the human use of fossil fuels."]}],"chars":5211},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bhutan":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"09bfbfabe44a62296c079a36b96fd1fcb8aeb70b8d7d81639f4d2153c3aa0e75","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/bhutan","bytes":39005,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Bhutan travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2012-12-20T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2025-12-10T13:09:24+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bhutan/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Bhutan’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Bhutan set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, see the ",["Bhutan government’s visa entry page","https://bhutan.travel/visa"]," or contact the ",["Bhutanese Embassy in Brussels","https://www.mfa.gov.bt/rbebrussels/ambassador/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you plan to leave Bhutan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to ."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual Citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to enter and leave Bhutan."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must apply for your visa in advance. The authorities will pre-approve the visa and issue it when you arrive in Bhutan."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can arrange a visa through a Bhutanese tour operator, through a Bhutanese hotel or directly through the ",["Department of Immigration’s website","https://visit.doi.gov.bt/"],". You will need to pay a non-refundable, one-off visa application fee of 40 US dollars."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling for business or other non-tourism reasons, you must arrange your visa through your sponsoring organisation in Bhutan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you get your passport stamped."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure the border control officer stamps your visa in your passport."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Permits"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have permits to travel to some states in Bhutan. Your tour guide will help to get these."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you want to extend your stay in Bhutan, go to the Department of Immigration in Thimphu to make a request."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Entry and exit points"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can enter or exit Bhutan by air through the international airport in Paro, or by the land entry point in Phuentsholing."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Bhutan guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/29/bhutan"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Sustainable development fee"]},{"k":"p","s":["All adult visitors must pay a ",["daily sustainable development fee","https://bhutan.travel/visa"]," (SDF) of 100 US dollars per night. There is a lower daily charge for children. Read more ",["information about the SDF","https://bhutan.travel/visa"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Bhutan. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to take antiques out of Bhutan. Customs officials may inspect items that appear to be antiques."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking tobacco into Bhutan"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can bring a small supply of tobacco for personal use. You will need to pay taxes and duties and be able to show proof of tax and duty payments if the authorities ask you to at any point during your visit."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into or out of Bhutan"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can take up to 30,000 Bhutan ngultrum into or out of Bhutan."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan to take foreign currency worth 10,000 US dollars or more into or out of Bhutan, you must declare it and get clearance from the Royal Monetary Authority of Bhutan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Indian rupees are widely accepted in Bhutan."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Bhutan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Bhutan, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crime levels are low across Bhutan, but you should take the same precautions as you would at home."]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep a copy of your passport’s photo page and visa, and your flight ticket separate from the originals when travelling."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Bhutanese people take their customs and traditions very seriously. Respect them at all times to avoid giving offence. Particularly avoid criticising HM The King of Bhutan. If in doubt, ask your tour guide."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dress code"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dress respectfully when visiting temples and Dzongs (fortified buildings, like castles), so that you do not cause offence. Your tour guide will be able to advise."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws"]},{"k":"p","s":["Alcohol is legal in Bhutan, but there are restrictions on how much alcohol tourists can buy at one time. Check with the vendor what the limit is."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Smoking and e-cigarette bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["It was illegal to sell or buy tobacco products in Bhutan until 2020. It is currently legal, but smoking is still frowned on. Be mindful of where you smoke – for example smoking near religious locations may cause offence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict penalties for possession, use and trafficking of illegal drugs. If convicted, you could get a prison sentence and heavy fine. Sentences range from a minimum of 3 years to a life sentence depending upon the type and quantity of drugs."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity was decriminalised in Bhutan in 2020, and there are no censorship laws restricting the discussion or promotion of LGBT+ topics. Same-sex marriages are not recognised. There is no legal recognition of transgender individuals."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildlife, animal products and souvenirs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Environmental conservation is critically important to Bhutan. You could be imprisoned for harming protected species. It is illegal to litter anywhere in Bhutan."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"p","s":["You need to use tour guides when visiting places of interest. Otherwise, you may be refused entry."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Mountaineering and hiking"]},{"k":"p","s":["Mountaineering is banned in Bhutan, but there are trekking options across the country at a wide range of altitudes. Take advice from your tour guide."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Bhutan, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Car rentals come with a driver. If you want to drive your own vehicle, you must hire a guide to travel with you."]},{"k":"p","s":["Any car you bring into Bhutan must meet the requirements of the ",["Bhutan Road Safety and Transport Authority","https://eralis.rsta.gov.bt/"],". You must have a driving licence, insurance documents, pollution control documents and an entry permit. You will need to pay a daily charge of 4,500 ngultrum. The same fees and rules apply for motorbikes."]},{"k":"p","s":["For a stay of more than 90 days, apply for a Bhutanese driving licence from the Bhutan Road Safety and Transport Authority. You must show your UK driving licence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Car and motorbike accidents are one of the biggest causes of injury and death in Bhutan. If possible, avoid travelling at night. Always travel in a well-maintained vehicle with seatbelts."]},{"k":"p","s":["Road conditions can be dangerous, particularly in monsoon season. There are no traffic lights in Bhutan."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Weather conditions regularly affect domestic and international flights."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Monsoon"]},{"k":"p","s":["Monsoon rains can cause landslides that cut off some roads for days. Always check your route before setting off and take extra care during the monsoon season."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Several parts of Bhutan lie on active fault zones. Limited emergency vehicles, equipment and medical facilities are likely to increase the impact of an earthquake. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildfires"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is high risk of wildfires, particularly in central and southern areas of the country. You will be fined if you cause a wildfire, even if it is accidental. The level of the fine increases if the wildfire is caused intentionally."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["Flooding, including flash flooding, can be caused by many natural events such as monsoon rains and earthquakes. Both rural and urban areas are vulnerable."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 112 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Bhutan","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/29/bhutan#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Bhutan","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/29/bhutan"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Bhutan. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re carrying a large amount of medicine or medicine that’s not for your personal use, check with the ",["Bhutanese Embassy in Brussels","https://www.mfa.gov.bt/rbebrussels/ambassador/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Bhutan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Healthcare facilities vary in quality across Bhutan. One hospital (Jigme Dorji Wangchuck National Referral Hospital) in Thimphu can provide surgery and emergency treatment. Outside of Thimphu, hospitals generally provide only basic healthcare. Treatment for more complex issues is not available in Bhutan and you would need evacuation to India or Thailand for treatment."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance that covers the cost of medical treatment abroad, emergency helicopter evacuation and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["English is widely spoken in Bhutan and doctors are likely to speak some English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Bhutan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 112"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 110"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 113"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["dealing with a death abroad","https://www.gov.uk/after-a-death/death-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["being arrested or imprisoned","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/arrested-or-detained-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/bhutan/british-high-commission-kolkata"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bhutan/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":12307,"change":"New information about dual nationals returning to the UK (‘Entry requirements’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/peak-polycrisis-why-trumps-midterm-drubbing-gives-us-reason-for-cautious-hope-296192":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"ce1d5a00c890c6df205430b96f8792adc9aa9e5eaa8d3184e1a1434337c2bb8e","read":"https://theconversation.com/peak-polycrisis-why-trumps-midterm-drubbing-gives-us-reason-for-cautious-hope-296192","bytes":189581,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Peak polycrisis? Why Trump’s midterm drubbing gives us reason for cautious hope","by":[{"n":"Andrew Heffernan","r":"Climate Associate at the Information Integrity Lab and Adjunct Professor in Political Studies, L’Université d’Ottawa/University of Ottawa"}],"pub":"2026-11-10T12:57:13Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["For the better part of a decade, reading the news has felt like watching a pile-up in slow motion. A pandemic. Wars in Ukraine, Gaza and Sudan. A cost-of-living squeeze that never quite eases. Wildfire smoke settling over Canadian cities. And the climate numbers keep setting records nobody wanted: according to the EU’s Copernicus service, 2023 to 2025 was ",["the first three-year stretch to average more than 1.5 C above pre-industrial levels.","https://www.rte.ie/news/world/2026/0114/1552984-climate-change-report"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Scholars have a word for this tangle of overlapping, mutually reinforcing shocks: the polycrisis. It’s an accurate and exhausting word."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["‘Polycrisis’ may be a buzzword, but it could help us tackle the world’s woes","https://theconversation.com/polycrisis-may-be-a-buzzword-but-it-could-help-us-tackle-the-worlds-woes-195280"]]},{"k":"p","s":["So let me say something in the aftermath of the midterm elections in the United States that may sound naive. I think we may have passed peak polycrisis."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Not because the problems are going away","https://theconversation.com/el-nino-2026-27-as-a-polycrisis-what-happens-when-health-and-energy-systems-fail-simultaneously-294109"],". Most of them will get worse. Climate change does not negotiate, wars do not end on schedule and the next pandemic is a question of when. What I think may have peaked is something else: the political dysfunction that made all of this so much harder to govern."]},{"k":"h","s":["A long view of bad times"]},{"k":"p","s":["Humans have always lived with shocks they did not choose. Plague, famine, war, depression. What has varied across history is whether societies could pull together to manage them. The institutions built after the Second World War in 1945 were not designed by people who thought the world was safe. They were designed by people who had just seen how bad things could get and decided co-operation was worth the trouble."]},{"k":"p","s":["That capacity to work together is precisely what’s eroded over the past decade. Right-wing populism spread across democracies by turning frustration into grievance, and grievance into contempt for experts, institutions and anyone on the other side."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["The ‘freedom convoy’ protesters are a textbook case of ‘aggrieved entitlement’","https://theconversation.com/the-freedom-convoy-protesters-are-a-textbook-case-of-aggrieved-entitlement-176791"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Trust collapsed. This year’s Edelman Trust Barometer found that ",["70 per cent of people worldwide are unwilling or hesitant to trust someone with different values.","https://www.edelman.com/news-awards/2026-edelman-trust-barometer-society-slides-into-insularity"]," In Canada, the figure is 73 per cent, and only 16 per cent of Canadians expect the next generation to be better off."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s impossible to govern a polycrisis under those conditions. Climate policy, pandemic preparedness and trade all depend on people accepting a shared set of facts and accepting that losing an argument is not the end of the world. Populism attacks both requirements."]},{"k":"h","s":["Global shifts"]},{"k":"p","s":["Which is why the U.S. midterms matter. American voters handed President Donald Trump a sweeping rebuke, ",["giving Democrats control of both the House and the Senate.","https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/election-day-2026-midterms/"]," Democrats flipped at least seven Senate seats, including Ohio, North Carolina, Iowa and even Kansas and South Carolina. Susan Collins lost her Senate seat in Maine, and in Texas of all places, James Talarico beat Ken Paxton. With races in Alaska and Mississippi still too close to call, ",["Democrats will hold at least 54 Senate seats.","https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/senate-election-results-2026/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["One midterm, on its own, proves little. The president’s party usually loses ground. But this one doesn’t stand alone."]},{"k":"p","s":[["In April, Hungarians ended Viktor Orbán’s 16 years in power","https://www.rferl.org/a/hungarian-opposition-leader-magyar-landslide-victory-orban/33730633.html"],", giving Péter Magyar’s Tisza party 53.6 per cent of the vote to the Fidesz party’s 37.8. Orbán was never just another populist. He was the model, the leader the international right flew to Budapest to learn from."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Lula da Silva also defeated Flávio Bolsonaro in the recent presidential runoff","https://kuwaittimes.com/article/52394/world/lula-wins-4th-term-as-flavio-bolsonaro-vows-to-seek-annulment/"],", 51.8 to 48.2 per cent."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Hungary turns the page into uncertainty after Péter Magyar ends Viktor Orbán’s enduring rule","https://theconversation.com/hungary-turns-the-page-into-uncertainty-after-peter-magyar-ends-viktor-orbans-enduring-rule-280656"]]},{"k":"p","s":["In Britain, Reform UK looked unstoppable a year ago. Since ",["Andy Burnham replaced Keir Starmer as prime minister this summer","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/9/30/burnham-bounce-why-labours-rising-again-reforms-slipping"],", Labour led every voting intention poll conducted in October, while ",["Reform slid from around 30 per cent to roughly 22.","https://leftfootforward.org/2026/11/labour-lead-every-single-opinion-poll-carried-out-in-october/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["In Israel, ",["Benjamin Netanyahu’s long hold on power may finally be slipping","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/29/israel-election-result-shows-no-overall-majority-as-vote-count-complete"],". His right-wing and religious bloc fell short of a majority in the recent election, winning only 53 of 120 seats, while Arab-led parties won a record 19."]},{"k":"p","s":["When President Isaac Herzog consulted the new Knesset, ",["67 lawmakers recommended challenger Gadi Eisenkot and only 46 backed Netanyahu","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/7/israels-president-picks-eisenkot-over-netanyahu-to-form-next-government"],", and Herzog gave Eisenkot the first chance to form a government."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Can Gadi Eisenkot turn the ‘disaster bloc’ into Israel’s next government?","https://theconversation.com/can-gadi-eisenkot-turn-the-disaster-bloc-into-israels-next-government-295859"]]},{"k":"p","s":["And in Canada, ",["Mark Carney’s approval sits at 65 per cent","https://press.liaisonstrategies.ca/federal-tracker-liberal-lead-narrows-to-13-points-october-26-2026/"],", a remarkable number for a prime minister a year and a half into the job. Opposition leader Pierre Poilievre, whose brand rests on the claim that Canada is broken, is viewed unfavourably by 52 per cent of Canadians in the same poll."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a pattern here. After a decade of rage politics, voters in very different countries seem to be reaching again for competence and something closer to normal."]},{"k":"h","s":["Taking on the social media accelerant"]},{"k":"p","s":["Something else has changed too. The platforms that pour fuel on the polarization flames no longer operate in a regulatory vacuum."]},{"k":"p","s":["Late ",["last year, the European Commission fined social media platform X 120 million euros for breaching its transparency obligations","https://ec.europa.eu/commission/presscorner/detail/en/ip_25_2934"],", the first penalty issued under the Digital Services Act."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Australia’s restrictions on social media accounts for those under 16 years old have been in force since December 2025","https://esafety.gov.au/about-us/industry-regulation/social-media-age-restrictions"],". After years of hearings and white papers, regulating big tech has moved from talk to enforcement."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Australia’s social media ban has an enforcement problem. These new laws aim to fix it","https://theconversation.com/australias-social-media-ban-has-an-enforcement-problem-these-new-laws-aim-to-fix-it-291356"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Hope, with fine print"]},{"k":"p","s":["None of this calls for a victory lap."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Brazil, ",["Lula won by under four points, and his opponent has vowed to seek an annulment","https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/10/25/world/brazil-election"],". In the U.K., Reform still polls above 20 per cent and ",["some predict the Burnham bounce will fade","https://www.telegraph.co.uk/politics/2026/10/27/hundred-days-andy-burnham-bounce-peaked/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Trump remains president for two more years, veto pen in hand, and ",["has made the most fiery hardliner in his administration, Stephen Miller","https://www.ctvnews.ca/world/article/trump-replaces-susie-wiles-with-stephen-miller-as-chief-of-staff-after-gops-midterm-defeat/"],", his chief of staff."]},{"k":"p","s":["The grievances that populists exploited are real and unresolved: housing, wages, the sense of being left behind. And the polycrisis carries on regardless of who wins elections."]},{"k":"p","s":["Cautious optimism is still optimism, though. The shocks may not be over, but our ability to respond to them, together, may be returning. ",["Historically, like in the post-Second World War period, that’s mattered most","https://psyche.co/ideas/from-wars-to-pandemics-people-in-crisis-need-to-feel-connected"]," during crises."]},{"k":"p","s":["For those of us who work on democracy, information integrity and multilateral co-operation, this is no time to ease off. It is a moment to press the advantage: to rebuild trust, shore up the institutions that let us govern shared problems and make the case once more that working together beats tearing each other apart."]},{"k":"p","s":["The problems are not getting smaller. But for the first time in a while, we may be getting better at facing them."]}],"chars":6651},"https://theconversation.com/pejabat-bukan-gen-alpha-asbun-mereka-saat-asap-karhutla-bukan-salah-ucap-tapi-krisis-empati-294869":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"6564157f856d755a687bcc6c462b6e3c2c8386f8954e2dfae372926d21449c30","read":"https://theconversation.com/pejabat-bukan-gen-alpha-asbun-mereka-saat-asap-karhutla-bukan-salah-ucap-tapi-krisis-empati-294869","bytes":177808,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Pejabat bukan Gen Alpha: ‘Asbun’ mereka saat asap karhutla bukan salah ucap, tapi krisis empati","by":[{"n":"Khairani","r":"Lecturer and Researcher, Member of Digital Services Marketing Research Cluster FEBUI, Universitas Indonesia"},{"n":"Inta Hartaningtyas Rani","r":"Dr./ Manajer Riset dan Media CHED ITB Ahmad Dahlan, Institut Teknologi dan Bisnis Ahmad Dahlan"}],"pub":"2026-11-03T04:00:41Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["● Pejabat daerah gagal menunjukkan empati dan keseriusan dalam merespons krisis karhutla."]},{"k":"p","s":["● Lelucon di tengah bencana merusak kepercayaan publik terhadap pemerintah."]},{"k":"p","s":["● Komunikasi krisis harus mengutamakan keselamatan, empati, dan kredibilitas informasi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kabut asap kembali menyelimuti sebagian Sumatra dan Kalimantan. Di Kotawaringin Barat, Kalimantan Tengah, BMKG setempat mencatat kualitas udara masuk ",["kategori sangat berbahaya","https://www.antaranews.com/berita/5770688/bmkg-sebut-kualitas-udara-di-palembang-di-level-sangat-berbahaya"],". Warga mengeluhkan sesak napas, batuk, dan mata perih."]},{"k":"p","s":["Di tengah situasi itu, Gubernur Kalimantan Tengah Agustiar Sabran justru melontarkan pelesetan ",["“bersatu kita teguh, bercerai kita kawin lagi”","https://news.detik.com/berita/d-8704537/pkb-kritik-gubernur-kalteng-bercanda-bercerai-kawin-lagi-soal-karhutla"]," saat ditanya soal penanganan kebakaran hutan dan lahan (karhutla)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Di Sumatra Selatan, Wali Kota Palembang Ratu Dewa, menanggapi pertanyaan soal kondisinya di tengah asap dengan menjawab ",["“mungkin saya enjoy-enjoy aja”","https://www.detik.com/sumbagsel/berita/d-8691515/ratu-dewa-sebut-asap-di-palembang-kiriman-dari-ogan-ilir-OKI-dan-banyuasin"],". Padahal kondisi di Palembang juga parah, ",["BMKG mencatat","https://www.bmkg.go.id/kualitas-udara/pm25/pm25_pl3"]," konsentrasi PM2.5 mencapai 554 µg/m³ pada 5 Oktober 2026, lebih dari dua kali ambang kategori berbahaya. Bahkan hingga 20 Oktober 2026, asap pekat masih mengepung Kota Palembang."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ucapan di atas kerap kita kenal sebagai ‘asbun’, alias asal bunyi yang mudah dianggap sebagai keseleo lidah. Namun, dalam kacamata komunikasi krisis, asbun adalah kegagalan komunikasi publik."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam situasi darurat, pejabat merupakan bagian dari komunikasi krisis yang seharusnya membantu warga memahami bahaya dan melindungi diri, bukan melontarkan lelucon."]},{"k":"h","s":["Humor yang salah tempat"]},{"k":"p","s":["Teori ",["Situational Crisis Communication (SCCT)","https://link.springer.com/article/10.1057/palgrave.crr.1550049"]," menyebutkan bahwa respons pihak berwenang harus sepadan dengan tingkat tanggung jawab yang dilekatkan publik kepadanya. Berdasarkan teori tersebut, prioritas pertama dalam krisis adalah melindungi warga dari bahaya, bukan menjaga citra organisasi—dalam konteks ini atau pemerintah."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pemerintah seharusnya mengarahkan masyakarat agar bisa melindungi diri (instructing information). Misalnya menghimbau penggunaan masker, atau ungkapan kepedulian bagi warga yang terdampak. Bukan asal menyeletuk dengan dalih melucu."]},{"k":"p","s":["Karhutla bukan kejadian baru, bencana ini berulang hampir setiap kemarau dan sudah seharusnya bisa dicegah atau diredam dampaknya baik oleh pemerintah daerah ataupun pemerintah pusat."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam SCCT, krisis yang bisa dicegah dan punya riwayat berulang menuntut strategi membangun kembali (rebuild): mengakui masalah, menunjukkan kepedulian, dan menjelaskan tindakan perbaikan. Jawaban ‘asbun’ justru menunjukkan sikap menyangkal (denial) atau mengecilkan (diminish) masalah."]},{"k":"p","s":["Padahal, ",["penelitian tahun 2020","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33132966/"]," menunjukkan bahwa penanganan krisis yang efektif sangat membutuhkan keyakinan warga bahwa pemerintah mampu melindungi mereka."]},{"k":"p","s":["Di Indonesia, pola komunikasi yang buruk memang terus berulang. Saat pandemi COVID-19, Menteri Kesehatan kala itu, Terawan Agus Putranto, mengatakan “enjoy saja, makan yang cukup”. ",["Riset tahun 2022","https://journal.ugm.ac.id/jsp/article/view/66443"]," tentang bagaimana komunikasi pemerintah Indonesia selama pandemi COVID-19 mencatat narasi pemerintah saat itu cenderung menyepelekan ancaman."]},{"k":"p","s":["Riset tersebut juga menggolongkan metafora pejabat yang merendahkan sebagai bad language, yaitu bahasa yang lahir dari pola pikir buruk dan berpotensi menyakiti. Pelesetan “bersatu kita teguh, bercerai kita kawin lagi” masuk dalam pola yang sama."]},{"k":"h","s":["Apa yang perlu dibenahi?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Komunikasi krusial dalam manajemen krisis, termasuk krisis kesehatan. Pusat Pengendalian dan Pencegahan Penyakit Amerika Serikat (Centers for Disease Control and Prevention/CDC) menyediakan pelatihan khusus Crisis and Emergency Risk Communication (CERC). Pelatihan ini ditujukan tidak hanya kepada tenaga kesehatan, tetapi juga kepada para pemimpin agar dapat berkomunikasi dengan baik dalam kondisi bahaya dan darurat."]},{"k":"p","s":["CERC juga memberikan panduan bagaimana berinteraksi dengan media, di antaranya be first (terdepan), be right (terbenar), dan be credible (terpercaya). Jawaban ‘asbun’ jelas tidak sesuai dengan panduan ini dan hanya akan membuat masyarakat meragukan kredibilitas penanganan krisis dan bencana."]},{"k":"p","s":["Padahal, Pasal 26 ayat 1 ",["UU Penanggulangan Bencana","https://peraturan.bpk.go.id/Details/39901/uu-no-24-tahun-2007"]," menempatkan rasa aman dan akses terhadap informasi kebijakan penanggulangan bencana sebagai hak setiap orang, bukan hadiah penguasa."]},{"k":"p","s":[["UU Keterbukaan Informasi Publik","https://jdih.komdigi.go.id/produk_hukum/view/id/172/t/undangundang%2Bnomor%2B14%2Btahun%2B%2B2008%2Btanggal%2B30%2Bapril%2B2008?search=permendagri+perlindungan+data+pribadi&utm_source=chatgpt.com"]," juga menegaskan: ketika ada ancaman terhadap hajat hidup orang banyak, badan publik wajib mengumumkannya serta-merta, dengan bahasa yang mudah dipahami ."]},{"k":"p","s":["Maka, ketika wartawan bertanya soal karhutla, yang berhak didengar warga adalah status bahaya, langkah penanganan, dan cara melindungi diri. Lelucon asbun tidak memuat satu pun dari ketiganya."]},{"k":"p","s":["Komunikasi krisis harus jujur, terbuka, cepat, akurat, dan lengkap. Sikap menyangkal atau mengecilkan krisis justru menggerus kredibilitas dan memperbesar dampak buruknya."]},{"k":"p","s":["Saat krisis, warga butuh informasi agar bisa bertindak tepat: cara menghindari bahaya, gejala yang perlu diwaspadai, dan ke mana harus berobat. Pemerintah perlu menunjuk juru bicara dan kanal resmi sejak awal, sekaligus menyampaikan empati kepada masyarakat, bukan melontarkan lelucon asbun."]}],"chars":4978},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/comoros":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"c9731b46a73e66fe60deae059371fa238f2c0524da72e6294f4ec548c569e5d7","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/comoros","bytes":40220,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Comoros travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2012-12-18T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2025-12-10T13:42:55+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/comoros/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Comoros’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Comoros set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the Comoros Embassy in Paris (in French)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Comoros, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to enter or travel through Comoros. You can buy a visa for 30 euros when you arrive at Hahaya airport or other points of entry."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Comoros guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/54/comoros#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Comoros","https://douane.gov.km/en/dedouanement.php"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Comoros"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Comoros, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Protests and unrest can happen in Comoros, including in Moroni and other parts of Grande Comore, Anjouan and Mohéli, particularly following elections. Protests have previously blocked roads, making travel in Moroni difficult, including between the city and the international airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["In January 2024, a protestor was killed and several injured in clashes with security forces."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid crowds and demonstrations and follow the advice and instructions of local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Due to a longstanding dispute between Comoros and France about the island of Mayotte, there is some anti-French sentiment in Comoros and occasional demonstrations on the issue. Monitor local media to keep up to date with developments."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crime levels are low but take precautions against pickpocketing. Street crime such as robbery is rare. Walking alone at night increases your risk, including on beaches or in town centres."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep your valuables, cash and important documents in hotel safes where possible."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always travel with your ID. Keep printed copies of your passport’s photo page and visa stamp."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Religion"]},{"k":"p","s":["Comoros is an Islamic country. The official religion is Sunni Islam. People are not allowed to practise Shia Islam in Comoros."]},{"k":"p","s":["Respect local traditions, customs, laws and religious practices. Make sure you do not offend cultural or religious beliefs."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dress and behaviour codes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Clothing for men and women needs to cover the body loosely, from the shoulders to the knees."]},{"k":"p","s":["Islanders mostly consider outward displays of intimacy to be contrary to public decency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["All matters of religious practice and custom are given particular importance by the people and authorities throughout the year. This importance is especially heightened during the month of Ramadan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year and country. Check the year’s Ramadan dates before you travel. During this time of Ramadan do not:"]},{"k":"li","s":["eat, drink, smoke or chew gum in public in the daytime, including in your car or in public view"]},{"k":"li","s":["play loud music or dance"]},{"k":"li","s":["swear in public"]},{"k":"p","s":["Get more advice when you arrive from your tour guide, hotel or business contacts."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check opening hours of shops and restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that if hotels and restaurants are providing food or drink in fasting hours, they may separate you from Islamic guests, for example with screens"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow local dress codes – clothing that does not meet local dress codes may cause more offence at this time"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that fasting can cause tiredness, particularly during the later afternoon and early evening"]},{"k":"li","s":["be patient and show tolerance"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws and bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is possible to buy alcohol in Comoros, for example at hotels, but drinking alcohol or being drunk on public highways is illegal. Offences are punishable by fines or even imprisonment."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pay particular attention to these rules during the Ramadan period."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Drug trafficking and possession are serious offences. If you are found guilty, you could get a long prison sentence and a fine."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is advisable to ask people for permission before photographing them. Avoid taking photos of public buildings, particularly military and police buildings."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is illegal in Comoros. If convicted you could get a prison sentence of up to 5 years and heavy fines."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are very few banks or ATMs in Grande Comore or on the other islands. People in Comoros mainly use cash. Credit cards are not always accepted – check in advance if your hotel accepts your card."]},{"k":"p","s":["Technical or connection issues with equipment may also make it difficult to pay by card so always have cash available. Some hotels and restaurants accept foreign currencies such as euros. However, they will give you change in Comorian francs."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Comoros, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Comoros for up to 3 months. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you need an extension after 3 months, go to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs at Rue du place de l’indépendance des Comores à Moroni or visit their Facebook page: ",["Ministère des Affaires Etrangères de l’Union des Comores","https://www.facebook.com/people/Minist%C3%A8re-des-Affaires-Etrang%C3%A8res-de-lUnion-des-Comores/100064519133618/?mibextid=ZbWKwL"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["On Grande Comore, the main ring-road is of a reasonable standard, but many other roads are in poor condition."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Boats and ferries take passengers between the 3 islands. They can be overloaded, in poor condition and without life jackets. Overloaded vessels have capsized in Comorian waters with significant loss of life."]},{"k":"p","s":["Recent attacks off the coast of Somalia and the Gulf of Aden highlight the significant risk of piracy and armed robbery."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling by sea, ",["read about the regional risks at sea","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/sea-river-and-piracy-safety"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tropical cyclones"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tropical cyclones can affect Comoros between January and May. Monitor local news and check ",["World Meteorological Organization weather reports for Comoros","https://severeweather.wmo.int/tc/swi/index.html"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Volcanic eruptions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Karthala, near Moroni on Grande Comore, is an active volcano which last erupted in 2007. Check ",["Karthala’s most recent reports and monitoring","https://volcano.si.edu/volcano.cfm?vn=233010"]," before you make plans to visit."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call hospitals and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"li","s":["Grande Comore, hopital El Maarouf: +269 773 26 04"]},{"k":"li","s":["Mohéli, hopital de Fomboni: +269 772 03 73"]},{"k":"li","s":["Anjouan, hopital de Hombo: +269 771 00 34"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Comoros","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/54/comoros#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Comoros","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/54/comoros"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Comoros"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical facilities on all 3 islands of Comoros are basic and most are private. Disruptions to electricity and water supplies can affect hospitals and other public services."]},{"k":"p","s":["Makes sure you have adequate travel insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical facilities in Comoros","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/comoros-doctors"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Comoros"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 113 or 114"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 117"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/what-to-do-after-a-british-national-dies-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/arrested-or-detained-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/comoros/british-embassy-antanarivo"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/comoros/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":11457,"change":"New information about dual nationals returning to the UK (‘Entry requirements’ page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/panama":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"217aa091e12ab82360b6bb43676e711cdb3fbee8d9621a27d056beb3b8af4b25","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/panama","bytes":67722,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Panama travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-21T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-10-09T21:08:09+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Earthquake"]},{"k":"p","s":["On 9 October 2026, a strong earthquake of preliminary magnitude 7.6 struck Panama. According to the Instituto de Geociencias de la Universidad de Panamá, the earthquake was recorded at a depth of 10 kilometres, approximately 39 kilometres west of Tonosí. The tremor was felt across much of the country and authorities are assessing damage."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are affected and need assistance from the UK government, call:"]},{"k":"p","s":["• From Panama: +507 297 6550 • From the UK: +44 (0) 20 7008 5000"]},{"k":"p","s":["Initial tsunami warnings have been lifted. Individuals in coastal areas should remain vigilant, follow instructions from local authorities, and move away from the shoreline if advised to do so."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be aware of the possibility of aftershocks and continue to follow local safety advice. We are monitoring the situation closely and will update this message as more information becomes available."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/panama/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Panama’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Panama set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Embassy and Consulate of Panama in the UK","https://www.panamaembassy.co.uk/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are visiting Panama, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the day you plan to leave Panama."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you live in Panama, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the day you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your passport must have at least one blank page."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Checks at border control"]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you get your passport stamped."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure immigration officials stamp your passport with the date you arrived in the country."]},{"k":"p","s":["At Panamanian border control, you may need to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["give the address of your accommodation and a contact telephone number"]},{"k":"li","s":["show a return or onward ticket – particularly if you arrive by land from Costa Rica and are not a legal resident of Costa Rica"]},{"k":"li","s":["prove you have at least 1000 US dollars (or the same amount in other currencies) or a credit card"]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Panama for up to 3 months without a visa if you arrive by land or air. There are different visa requirements for sea arrivals."]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot normally extend your stay, unless you apply to change your immigration status (for example, for business purposes or marriage) within the 3 months."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you try to extend your stay by visiting a neighbouring country and returning to Panama, immigration officials may detain you. The British Embassy cannot intervene in decisions made by Panama’s immigration officials."]},{"k":"hs","s":["If you arrive by sea"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you arrive on a vessel that is not a cruise ship, you must have a visa to enter Panama. You must pay a fee of 100 US dollars, plus 5 US dollars registration, for each passenger or crew member. There may be other fees, for example for cruising permits. Check in advance what permits you will need and how to get them."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you arrive on a cruise ship or are travelling through the Panama Canal, you do not need a visa unless you are staying in Panama for more than 3 months. Immigration authorities will stamp your passport if you leave the ship. They do not board cruise ships travelling through the Canal to check passports."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you need a visa, apply through the ",["Embassy and Consulate of Panama in the UK","https://panamaembassy.co.uk/"],". They can give you more information on entry requirements."]},{"k":"p","s":["For information on extending your stay, check with the ",["Panama National Migration Service","https://www.migracion.gob.pa/"]," (in Spanish)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Airport tax"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a charge of 40 US dollars on departure. This is usually included in the price of your ticket. Check with your airline."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Panama, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Panama guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/174/panama#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Panama. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Panama"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there is no recent history of terrorism in Panama, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Protests and demonstrations"]},{"k":"p","s":["Protests can be unpredictable, occur at short notice and escalate quickly. Avoid protests and demonstrations, monitor local media and follow advice from local authorities. Avoid travelling around protest-affected areas at night. Protests may be particularly large in Colón City."]},{"k":"p","s":["Protests often involve informal road blocks and can affect access to the border crossing into Costa Rica at Paso Canoas and international airports. Check your route and alternatives before travelling. If you are unable to reach an airport for a planned flight, contact your airline to make alternative arrangements."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are the victim of a crime in Panama and want to report the incident, do so before you leave the country, otherwise the police may not investigate."]},{"k":"p","s":["Street crime can happen anywhere, but these areas of Panama City have higher levels of crime:"]},{"k":"li","s":["San Miguelito"]},{"k":"li","s":["El Chorrillo"]},{"k":"li","s":["Río Abajo"]},{"k":"li","s":["24 de Diciembre"]},{"k":"li","s":["Santa Ana"]},{"k":"li","s":["Juan Diaz"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of pickpocketing in busy areas, on buses and at bus stations. You can take steps to protect yourself and your belongings, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["not carrying large amounts of money or valuables around with you"]},{"k":"li","s":["leaving valuables in a safe place such as a hotel safe"]},{"k":"p","s":["People have been attacked after withdrawing cash from ATMs. Where possible, use an ATM inside a bank or shopping centre."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take sensible precautions to avoid mugging, particularly in main shopping areas and tourist sites, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Albrook Mall in Panama City"]},{"k":"li","s":["Via España and Avenida Central in Panama City"]},{"k":"li","s":["the area of Calidonia in Panama City"]},{"k":"li","s":["the old town (Casco Viejo) in Panama City"]},{"k":"li","s":["the old Panama ruins (Panama Viejo) in Panama City"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Madden Dam area – off the main Panama to Colón road"]},{"k":"li","s":["the city of Colón"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be wary if visitors approach you to get access to your accommodation. Criminal gangs have used this method to commit burglaries. If you’re in any doubt, call the police."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been violent attacks, including sexual assault, in tourist destinations in Panama City and across the country. Use the same level of caution you would in the UK when travelling at night. Avoid poorly lit areas and do not walk on your own."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["advice for women travelling abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Gang-related crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been incidents of targeted gang assassinations, some in tourist areas. Most of these crimes are between members of rival drug gangs."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["As a foreign national, you must carry ID such as a passport. The police will usually accept a printed copy."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Curfews"]},{"k":"p","s":["Local authorities occasionally impose night-time curfews for adults and/or unaccompanied minors under the age of 18. These are usually in place for several weeks and limited exceptions apply. This is part of government efforts to tackle criminal groups and organised crime."]},{"k":"p","s":["Those who do not comply with the curfew face arrest by the police. They are not usually applied in tourist areas, but seek local advice if a curfew is introduced in an area you are visiting."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Smoking and e-cigarette bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to smoke in public places. You could be fined 25 to 100 US dollars if you are caught smoking where it’s not allowed. The use of e-cigarettes is also banned in public places."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not become involved with drugs of any kind. You can get a prison sentence for possessing even a small quantity of drugs."]},{"k":"p","s":["The judicial process is slow and sentencing may take up to 2 years, during which you are likely to be detained. Conditions in prisons and other detention facilities in Panama are often harsh. Most facilities are overcrowded with limited access to healthcare. There have been recent cases of riots resulting in prisoner deaths."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex civil unions are illegal, but same-sex relationships are legal in Panama. Most Panamanians are generally tolerant of LGBT+ travellers. However, Panamanian law does not ban discrimination based on sexual orientation and gender identity. There have been incidents of police officers detaining LGBT+ couples on the grounds of public indecency. Showing affection in public can lead to unwanted attention. Casco Viejo is considered a safe place for LGBT+ travellers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care when wading, swimming or taking part in water sports on Pacific and Caribbean beaches. Some beaches have strong currents and undertows and there are rarely warning signs. People drown every year."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not swim in the Bay of Panama as it is highly polluted with untreated sewage and industrial waste."]},{"k":"p","s":["See advice on ",["safe swimming from ABTA","https://www.abta.com/tips-and-advice/staying-safe-on-holiday/swim-safe"]," and ",["holiday water safety from the Royal Life Saving Society","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hiking and mountaineering"]},{"k":"p","s":["If hiking in Panama you should consider going with an experienced guide. Trails may not be well marked, and mobile phone coverage is unreliable. Tourists have gone missing and died hiking without a guide. Seek local advice before setting out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning on driving in Panama, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Panama for up to 3 months. The Panamanian authorities will not accept a paper licence – you can ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"],". Carry a copy of your passport with the dated entry stamp as proof you’re still within the 3 months permitted."]},{"k":"p","s":["Drivers and front-seat passengers must wear seatbelts. Children aged 4 and under must travel in the back in fitted child seats."]},{"k":"p","s":["Drink-driving is a serious offence in Panama. If you are tested and found to have any alcohol in your system, you may get a fine, have your licence revoked and your car impounded."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving standards"]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving standards can be poor. Traffic accidents are common. Roads are often poorly lit and can have potholes and unfinished repairs. Darien Province and other remote rural areas may have very few surfaced roads."]},{"k":"p","s":["Traffic can be heavy in populated areas especially in and close to Panama City."]},{"k":"p","s":["Repair work and construction sites are common in these areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are involved in a traffic accident with another driver, wait inside your vehicle for your insurance representative and the traffic police to arrive. Avoid any type of confrontation with other drivers or passers-by."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Taxis can be in poor condition and accidents, due to poor maintenance and driving standards, are common. To reduce your risk, use ride-hailing apps or hotel-arranged transport only."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"]," for information about how to prepare, and how to react if there is a warning."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hurricanes"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Atlantic hurricane season runs from June to November. Hurricanes do not directly affect Panama but often cause heavy rain. There may be flash floods and landslides. October and November have the heaviest rainfall."]},{"k":"p","s":["Monitor local news, check ",["World Meteorological Association weather reports for Panama","https://worldweather.wmo.int/en/country.html?countryCode=76"]," and follow local advice."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Earthquakes are a risk in Panama. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"]," or tsunami."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Panama. It only covers regions where FCDO has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/panama"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/panama/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Colombia border"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of violence near the Colombia border in an area east of a line drawn between:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Punta Carreto in the Comarca de Guna Yala on the Atlantic coast"]},{"k":"li","s":["Yaviza in the eastern Darien Province"]},{"k":"li","s":["Punta Piña on the Pacific coast"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should only travel to the east of this line in an organised group, and make sure local police and security authorities are aware of your visit. Follow local security advice and do not stray from your group."]},{"k":"p","s":["Colombian criminal violence can spill over into the region of Panama bordering Colombia where there is a threat from Colombian and other armed groups. Foreign nationals and Panamanian citizens have been the victims of violent crimes, kidnapping and murder in this area."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need;"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 103 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 911 for emergencies."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Panama","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/174/panama#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Panama","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/174/panama"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika virus"]},{"k":"li","s":["chikungunya"]},{"k":"li","s":["HIV"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tap water is safe to drink in most of the country. Follow local recommendations in rural and island areas, where there can be a risk of contaminated water."]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Panama. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Panama"]},{"k":"p","s":["Panama City has some good private hospitals and clinics, but medical facilities outside the capital are limited."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical providers in Panama","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/panama-list-of-lawyers/list-of-medical-facilitiespractitioners-in-panama-city"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Panama"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 911 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can also call specific emergency numbers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 103"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 103"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 104"]},{"k":"h","s":["Panamanian Tourism Authority"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: +507 6330 2520"]},{"k":"p","s":["Email: contact@atp.gob.pal"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Panama"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Panama"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Panama"]," in Panama"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Panama","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bereavement-information-for-panama"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Panama","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/panama-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/panama/british-embassy-panama-city"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/panama/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Panama","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-panama"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":17640,"change":"Information about a 7.6 earthquake in Panama (Warnings and insurance)"},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/somalia":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"804e449f918eae0015e9c7dd0a215d52d768357e7ba3c2c6abf061b53f27b790","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/somalia","bytes":64440,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Somalia travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-20T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-06-04T15:57:41+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Parts of Somalia, including Somaliland"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to Somalia, including Somaliland, except for the regions of Awdal, Maroodijeh, and Sahil."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the regions of Awdal, Maroodijeh, and Sahil."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is due to the threat from terrorist groups and continuing violence. If you choose to remain in Somalia, you do so at your own risk. You should have a personal emergency plan that does not rely on the UK government."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/somalia/regional-risks"],". There has recently been an increase in fighting between al-Shabaab and the Somali Government close to the capital Mogadishu. Please see the ",["Terrorism section","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/somalia/safety-and-security"]," for more information."]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["Support from FCDO is severely limited in Somalia, including Somaliland, with no support in person from staff at the British Embassy Mogadishu or the British Office Hargeisa."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you need urgent help from the UK government, for example if you’ve been arrested or you’re concerned about forced marriage, contact:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the ",["British High Commission Nairobi, Kenya","https://www.gov.uk/government/world/organisations/british-high-commission-nairobi"]," if you are in Somalia, excluding Somaliland"]},{"k":"li","s":["the ",["British Embassy Addis Ababa, Ethiopia","https://www.gov.uk/world/organisations/british-embassy-addis-ababa"]," if you are in Somaliland"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re in the UK and are concerned about a British national in Somalia, including Somaliland, call FCDO on 020 7008 5000."]},{"k":"h","s":["People of Somali descent, including Somaliland descent"]},{"k":"p","s":["The government of Somalia and the authorities in Somaliland will consider any British national of Somali (including Somaliland) descent to be a dual national. FCDO can offer only limited consular support in these cases."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/somalia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK, who choose to travel despite FCDO advice. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Somalia’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Somalia set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Somalian Embassy in the UK","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/foreign-embassies-in-the-uk"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Somalia, including Somaliland, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to enter Somalia, including Somaliland."]},{"k":"hs","s":["E-Visa data breach"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are reports of a data breach affecting Somalia’s eVisa system"]},{"k":"p","s":["Leaked data from the breach includes visa applicants’ names, photos, dates and places of birth, email addresses, marital status, and home addresses. This data breach is ongoing and could expose any personal data you enter into the system,"]},{"k":"p","s":["An eVisa is required before travelling to Somalia. Consider the risks before applying."]},{"k":"p","s":["US Embassy in Somalia have also issued an alert to US citizens. See - ",["Alert: Federal Republic of Somalia (FGS) Electronic Visa (E-Visa) Data Breach - U.S. Embassy in Somalia","https://so.usembassy.gov/alert-federal-republic-of-somalia-fgs-electronic-visa-e-visa-data-breach/?fbclid=IwdGRzaAODEvFjbGNrA4MS2mV4dG4DYWVtAjExAHNydGMGYXBwX2lkDDM1MDY4NTUzMTcyOAABHr_McNpy95Rny0OHFc1FVoE1scR89bh02jlwnxfc04XxpbksRE5PPkCKYQGh_aem_ORHiTkwZvd9alLjxfaj60g&sfnsn=scwspwa%3C/a"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are travelling to Mogadishu International Airport, you will need to apply for an ",["eVisa","https://etas.gov.so/"]," prior to your arrival."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are travelling to Hargeisa International Airport, you may still be asked to present this ",["eVisa","https://etas.gov.so/"]," in order to board your flight but it will not be considered valid for entry when you arrive in Hargeisa."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will need to purchase a single-entry visa upon arrival at Hargeisa International Airport, which will be valid for one month."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is not clear if you’ll be given a visa on arrival at other points of entry. Get confirmation from local authorities or your sponsoring organisation."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may also need to provide a letter of invitation when you arrive, outlining the reason for your visit. You can usually get this from your place of work. Without this letter, you may not be allowed to enter."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Somalia guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/200/somalia#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Somalia, including Somaliland. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"p","s":["Khat is a legal drug in Somalia, but it is an offence to take it out of the country. Officials regularly search bags at Hargeisa and Mogadishu airports, and anyone found to be in possession of khat is likely to face criminal prosecution."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into and out of Somalia (including Somaliland)"]},{"k":"p","s":["In Somaliland you must declare cash or travellers cheques if the value is 10,000 US dollars or more."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This guide also has safety advice for ",["regions of Somalia, including Somaliland","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/somalia/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Somalia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are very likely to try to carry out attacks in Somalia, including Somaliland."]},{"k":"p","s":["The terrorist group Al Shabaab, and other groups opposed to the Federal Government, continue to carry out frequent attacks, including in the capital Mogadishu. Terrorist groups operating in Somalia have made threats against westerners and those working for western organisations in Somalia, including Somaliland."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate and occur at any time, including in places visited by foreigners such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["embassies"]},{"k":"li","s":["government buildings"]},{"k":"li","s":["military bases"]},{"k":"li","s":["hotels and restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["transport hubs including the international airports and ports"]},{"k":"li","s":["crowded places"]},{"k":"li","s":["at high-profile events"]},{"k":"p","s":["Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities. The Somali Security Forces regularly carry out counter-terrorist operations against Al-Shabaab, mainly in central and southern Somalia. There has recently been a significant increase in conflict between al-Shabaab and Somali Security Forces in the Middle Shabelle region, and increased threats against Mogadishu security."]},{"k":"p","s":["Examples of previous significant attacks include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["In April 2025, there were multiple rocket attacks targeting Mogadishu International Airport and other sites."]},{"k":"li","s":["In March 2025, there was a significant improvised explosive device (IED) attack on the President’s convoy in Mogadishu. 16 people were reportedly killed but the President was unharmed."]},{"k":"li","s":["In February and March 2025 it was notable that two rocket attacks against Mogadishu Airport took place in daylight hours (historically, rocket attacks are more common at night)."]},{"k":"li","s":["In March 2025 there was an attack on Cairo Hotel in Beledweyne with more than six people killed."]},{"k":"li","s":["in August 2024, there was an attack on Lido Beach in Mogadishu with more than fifty civilians killed and over 200 injured"]},{"k":"li","s":["in July 2024, there was an attack on Top Coffee Restaurant in Mogadishu with many civilians reported killed and injured"]},{"k":"li","s":["in June 2023, there was an attack on the Pearl Beach Hotel at Lido Beach in Mogadishu with at least 9 civilians reported killed and 10 injured"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2022, 2 large improvised explosive devices (IEDs) were used to attack the Somali Ministry of Education, with over 100 civilians reported killed and 300 injured"]},{"k":"p","s":["While attacks occur less frequently in Somaliland, terrorists are still very likely to try to carry out attacks."]},{"k":"p","s":["The risk of attacks in Somalia, including Somaliland, may be further heightened during religious holidays."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorist kidnaps"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of kidnapping throughout Somalia, including in regions bordering Kenya and Ethiopia, and in Somaliland. Terrorists and criminal groups, including piracy groups, are involved in kidnapping. A number of western nationals, including British nationals, have been kidnapped in Somalia and some have been killed."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals are seen as legitimate targets, including tourists, humanitarian aid workers, journalists and business travellers. If you are kidnapped, the reason for your presence is unlikely to protect you or secure your safe release."]},{"k":"p","s":["The long-standing policy of the British government is to not make substantive concessions to hostage takers. The British government considers that paying ransoms and releasing prisoners builds the capability of terrorist groups and finances their activities. This can, in turn, increase the risk of further hostage-taking. The Terrorism Act (2000) makes payments to terrorists illegal."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are working or travelling in Somalia, including in Somaliland, you should be aware of the risk of kidnapping. You should maintain a high level of vigilance at all times, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["when travelling and at transport hubs"]},{"k":"li","s":["in crowded public places"]},{"k":"li","s":["in camps for displaced people"]},{"k":"li","s":["at religious gatherings and places of worship"]},{"k":"li","s":["in markets, shopping malls, hotels, bars and restaurants"]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you have carefully considered the threat and have reasonable, proportionate mitigation measures in place."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Somalia may see an increased risk of politically motivated unrest in the period around 15 May 2026. Past unrest has included protests and incidents of violence, including fatalities. On 3 June 2026, there were clashes in Mogadishu between Somali Security Forces and opposition forces."]},{"k":"p","s":["Political and community-based violence is common across Somalia, including Somaliland, and can flare up with little warning. Take care in public places where people gather. Monitor local and international media to help you avoid areas where demonstrations, protests, large crowds or disturbances are taking place. Leave any area of unrest quickly and do not attempt to watch or photograph it."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a dangerous level of criminal activity by armed militia throughout Somalia. There have been murders, armed robbery and criminal kidnaps."]},{"k":"p","s":["The humanitarian situation in Somalia has led to a large displacement of people, and a growth in refugee camps which are overpopulated. Food and health insecurity has led to an increase in crime, particularly around the refugee camps."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry your passport and visa with you as ID. Somali nationals should consult local authorities in Somalia on personal ID requirements."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year and country. During this time, do not:"]},{"k":"li","s":["eat, drink, smoke or chew gum in public in the daytime, including in your car"]},{"k":"li","s":["play loud music or dance"]},{"k":"li","s":["swear in public"]},{"k":"p","s":["Get more advice when you arrive from your tour guide, hotel or business contacts."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check opening hours of shops and restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that if hotels and restaurants are providing food or drink in fasting hours, they may separate you from Islamic guests, for example with screens"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow local dress codes – clothing that does not meet local dress codes may cause more offence at this time"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that fasting can cause tiredness, particularly during the later afternoon and early evening"]},{"k":"li","s":["be patient and show tolerance"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Public offences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Somalia has adopted Sharia law but is yet to implement it throughout the country. Al-Shabaab and other insurgent groups often have an extreme view on how to apply Sharia law."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s illegal for Somali Muslims to convert to another religion or promote any religion other than Islam."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws and bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["The drinking and sale of alcohol is banned in Somalia."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Drug offences, including drug use, possession and trafficking, are treated seriously in Somalia and are punishable by law. Possible punishments include a lengthy prison sentence without bail."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is illegal in Somalia. LGBT+ partners should not show affection in public."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money"]},{"k":"p","s":["Credit cards are not widely accepted in Somalia and it is not possible to get currency advances using a credit card. You should take cash with you into the country. The US dollar is the main currency for exchanging in Somalia."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Hargeisa you can withdraw US dollars from ATMs using international credit and debit cards."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Travelling by road in Somalia is dangerous and you should get advice from a security firm or a sponsoring organisation. Government forces, militias and other armed groups operate checkpoints on roads across Somalia. Exercise extreme caution when passing checkpoints and closely follow the instructions given by police and military personnel."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is still a significant risk of ",["piracy in the Gulf of Aden and Indian Ocean","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/sea-river-and-piracy-safety"],", where piracy has been reduced but not fully prevented. Pirates can attack up to 1,000 nautical miles from the Somali coast or more. The threat assessment of the combined international naval counter-piracy forces is that sailing yachts should not enter the ",["designated high-risk area,","https://on-shore.mschoa.org/"]," due to the risk of hijacking."]},{"k":"p","s":["Maritime crime and security incidents are also a risk in the Southern Red Sea area."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["The main rainy season in Somalia takes place between April and June, followed by lesser rains in October and November."]},{"k":"p","s":["Localised flooding may prevent you from getting to some parts of Somalia, including Somaliland."]},{"k":"p","s":["Flooding increases humanitarian need by forcing people to move or cutting them off from possible support. The end of 2023 saw widespread flooding in south-western Somalia, leading to significant internal displacement and disruption to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Somalia. It only covers regions where the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/somalia"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/somalia/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Togdheer, Sanaag and Sool"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) advises against all travel to the regions of Toghdeer, Sanaag and Sool in eastern Somaliland. There has been an increase in violent clashes in recent months and the situation remains volatile, so if you do travel, exercise extreme caution."]},{"k":"h","s":["Awdal, Maroodijeh and Sahil"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the 3 western regions of Somaliland – Awdal (including Boorama), Maroodijeh (including Hargeisa) and Sahil (including Berbera)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Border areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with local authorities before travelling to the border, and monitor travel advice for your destination: Ethiopia, Kenya or Djibouti. If you try to cross the border without the correct documents, officials may stop you."]},{"k":"p","s":["Land borders with countries neighbouring Somalia may close at short notice. You may get a fine or detention for illegally crossing borders. The land border with Kenya is currently closed due to recent cross border terrorist activity. There have been reports that foreign nationals have been prevented from crossing the Djiboutian border into Somalia, though the border remains open."]},{"k":"h","s":["The rest of Somalia"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to the rest of Somalia. There is ongoing, serious violence between opposing factions in many parts of the country. Civilians of all ages have been killed in fighting, which often involves heavy weapons."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 999 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["If that number does not work, call the Somali Red Crescent on 445 for emergency services."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest information on ",["vaccination recommendations in TravelHealthPro’s Somalia guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/200/somalia#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Somalia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/200/somalia"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["cholera"]},{"k":"li","s":["polio"]},{"k":"p","s":["The humanitarian situation in Somalia has led to a large displacement of people, and a growth in refugee camps which are overpopulated. This has led to health insecurity and an increase of exposure to disease, particularly around the refugee camps."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Somalia"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are basic hospital facilities in Hargeisa. Elsewhere, medical facilities are extremely limited and often at great distances. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad, evacuation by air ambulance and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Somalia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/somalia-medical-facilities/somalia-list-of-medical-facilities"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Somalia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 999"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 555"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 888"]},{"k":"p","s":["These emergency numbers can be unreliable. The Somali Red Crescent operates a free number for all emergency services on 446."]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Somalia"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Somalia"]]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Somalia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/somalia-bereavement-information/somalia-bereavement-information"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Somalia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/somalia-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/somalia/british-embassy-mogadishu"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/somalia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":20086,"change":"Updated information about the political situation ('Safety and security' page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/taiwan":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"aa5ac2fe7cf36a9c34191fdc04f4c12b54d98bc0ef761763d6f126e3f985b889","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/taiwan","bytes":76773,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Taiwan travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2012-12-20T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-08-28T13:31:24+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["The UK does not recognise Taiwan as a state and has no diplomatic relations with Taiwan, so limited support is available to British nationals. Please refer to the ",["British Office in Taipei","https://www.gov.uk/world/organisations/british-office-taipei"]," for further information."]},{"k":"h","s":["Typhoon season warning"]},{"k":"p","s":["Typhoons can affect Taiwan in June, but the most active period is between July and September. Typhoon frequency gradually decreases in October. If you are planning to visit Taiwan during typhoon season, it is important to stay informed and plan ahead:"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor official weather forecast: check the website of the Taiwan ",["Central Weather Administration","https://www.cwa.gov.tw/eng/"]," for updated typhoon news"]},{"k":"li","s":["be flexible with your itinerary: flights, trains, buses and other transportation services may be delayed or cancelled during severe weather"]},{"k":"li","s":["check your travel arrangements with your travel provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow the guidance of the Taiwanese authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["conditions may be dangerous for swimming, water sports and other activities in coastal waters around Taiwan during this period"]},{"k":"p","s":["Information and advice on how you can prepare for a range of disasters and emergency situations in Taiwan can be found in their Public Safety Guide or ",["“Little Orange Book”","https://adma.mnd.gov.tw/files/web/191/file_up/100004/1368/In%20Case%20of%20CrisisTaiwan%E2%80%99s%20National%20Public%20Safety%20Guide(Second%20Edition).pdf"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help British nationals make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/taiwan/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Taiwan’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Taiwan set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Taipei Representative Office in London","https://www.roc-taiwan.org/uk_en/index.html"]," or the ",["Taipei Representative Office in Edinburgh","https://www.roc-taiwan.org/ukedi_en/index.html"],". Entry procedures are being regularly reviewed, so may change at short notice."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Taiwan, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the day you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Arrival cards"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must complete a Taiwan Arrival Card (TWAC) within three days before your arrival in Taiwan. This must be submitted online via the ",["Ministry of the Interior National Immigration Agency","https://www.immigration.gov.tw/5475/"]," website."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may be exempt if you hold a resident visa, Alien Resident Card (ARC), Alien Permanent Resident Card (APRC), or other permits issued by the Taiwanese authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["For further advice and instructions on how to complete and submit the TWAC, check the ",["National Immigration Agency","https://twac.immigration.gov.tw/faq"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Taiwan without a visa for up to 90 days. You can extend this by a further 90 days once you have arrived in Taiwan. You can get more information on ",["entering Taiwan without a visa (‘visa-exempt entry’)","https://www.boca.gov.tw/cp-149-4486-7785a-2.html"]," from the Taiwan Bureau of Consular Affairs. This applies if you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["as a tourist"]},{"k":"li","s":["to visit family or friends"]},{"k":"li","s":["to attend business meetings, cultural or sports events"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan to stay in Taiwan for longer than 180 days, you must have a visa before you arrive. If you stay beyond the time given on your visa, you will get a fine and risk being deported from Taiwan."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are specific rules for naturalised British citizens born in the People’s Republic of China and holders of British National (Overseas) passports wishing to enter under the visa waiver scheme."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact the ",["Taiwan Bureau of Consular Affairs","https://www.boca.gov.tw/mp-2.html"]," or ",["Taiwan National Immigration Agency","https://www.immigration.gov.tw/5475/"]," for further information."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are in the UK and need a visa, apply at your nearest ",["Taipei Representative Office","https://www.roc-taiwan.org/uk_en/index.html"],". If you are in Taiwan, apply through the ",["Taiwan National Immigration Agency","https://www.immigration.gov.tw/5475/"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alien Resident Certificate and Alien Permanent Resident Certificate holders"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you already hold a resident certificate, you do not need a visa to enter Taiwan."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you hold a ",["Youth Mobility Scheme visa for Taiwan","https://www.roc-taiwan.org/ukedi_en/post/711.html"],", you can apply to switch to a working visa or a visa to study a degree course at undergraduate level or higher."]},{"k":"p","s":["Submit your application to the ",["Bureau of Consular Affairs","https://www.boca.gov.tw/mp-2.html"]," for consideration. If it is approved, you can then apply for an Alien Resident Certificate (ARC) at your local ",["National Immigration Agency (NIA) Service Center","https://www.immigration.gov.tw/5475/5478/141386/127061/127076/"],". Contact the ",["Bureau of Consular Affairs","https://www.boca.gov.tw/mp-2.html"]," or ",["National Immigration Agency","https://www.immigration.gov.tw/5475/"]," for further information."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Taiwan guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/218/taiwan#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Taiwan","https://web.customs.gov.tw/etaipei/singlehtml/3396?cntId=384c2899694f48038eba557cfc22ffd0"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Animal products"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not bring animal products into Taiwan without authorisation. If you are caught with any animal products, you may face a heavy fine. Customs officials have increased inspections due to concerns about African Swine Fever Virus in pork products, particularly from the People’s Republic of China."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Bringing money into Taiwan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare cash or travellers cheques if the value is higher than 100,000 New Taiwan dollars (NTD) or 10,000 US dollars. You will get a certified declaration to show you brought it in with you. If you do not, your money could be seized when you leave. Contact the ",["Customs Administration","https://web.customs.gov.tw/ekaohsiung/singlehtml/c718884d9be040dcb652112cdbabad3a?cntId=cb9e98e0aa664b4eb58f638076ddbeef"]," for further information."]},{"k":"p","s":["International bank transfers can be slow. Most of the ATMs in 7-11 stores accept international cards. Other ATMs may accept them, but not all do."]},{"k":"p","s":["American Express, Citibank and Thomas Cook branches accept their own-brand travellers cheques. You may need your receipt as well as your passport when you cash them."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Taiwan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Taiwan, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crisis preparedness"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Taiwanese authorities have provided ",["practical guidance and information","https://prepare.mnd.gov.tw/"]," (in Chinese), including a booklet, on disaster preparedness and responding to various crises."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crime rates are extremely low in Taiwan. However, travellers are advised to remain vigilant, monitor local media, and follow local law enforcement."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry ID such as a passport. The police will usually accept a printed copy of the photo page."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and penalties"]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid any involvement with illegal drugs, including cannabis, while in Taiwan. Drug laws are stricter than in the UK. Legal definitions of supply or trafficking may be different from in the UK, including the quantities of drugs involved."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re found guilty of smuggling, trafficking, possession or use of illegal narcotics, including when transiting through the airport, you should expect to get a severe prison sentence or, in some cases, the death penalty."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Taiwan have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Taiwan has some of Asia’s most progressive policies on LGBT+ rights, and discrimination on the grounds of gender and gender identity is illegal. Taiwan’s Pride parade, held annually in October, is the largest regular LGBT+ event in Asia, attracting high numbers of participants from the region and internationally."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Taiwan, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You need a 1949 ",["international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well as a UK driving licence to drive in Taiwan. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Once in Taiwan, you will need to take your passport, IDP and a passport photograph to a local Motor Vehicles Office to get your IDP validated. Your validated IDP will last up to 12 months."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you stay longer, you will need to get a new IDP and get it validated. Or you can exchange your UK driving licence for a Taiwan driving licence at a Motor Vehicles Office. The British Office in Taipei cannot provide support on individual applications."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you do not want to exchange your UK driving licence, you can take a local driving test to get a Taiwan driving licence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving standards and road rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["Roads and vehicles are well-maintained, but scooters and motorcycles often weave in and out of traffic. Be alert when crossing roads as vehicles might not stop at pedestrian crossings."]},{"k":"p","s":["The alcohol limit for drivers in Taiwan is about a quarter of that in England. If you drive while over the limit, you may get a heavy fine and possible imprisonment. If you are a passenger, you may also be fined."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If there is a typhoon or an earthquake, check the Taiwanese authorities’ websites for public announcements and details of which roads, schools and office buildings have been closed:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["Directorate-General of Personnel Administration","https://www.dgpa.gov.tw/typh/daily/ndse.html"]]},{"k":"li","s":["Directorate General of Highways"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Typhoons"]},{"k":"p","s":["The typhoon season in Taiwan normally runs from May to November. There’s a risk of road blockages and landslides after typhoons, especially in central and southern Taiwan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Listen to typhoon alerts on the ICRT, BCC and PRS radio stations, and monitor the websites of the ",["Central Weather Administration","https://www.cwa.gov.tw/eng/"]," and the Japan Meteorological Agency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Earthquakes are a risk in Taiwan. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency has guidance about what to do before, during and after an earthquake."]},{"k":"p","s":["Taipei City Government have created an ",["online digital booklet","https://www.eoc.gov.taipei/En_DisasterManual/mobile/index.html#p=1"]," with useful information on how to keep safe during an earthquake, typhoon and other types of natural and man-made disasters."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 119 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Unlike in the UK, an ambulance crew will not usually include a paramedic."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Taiwan","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/218/taiwan#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Taiwan","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/218/taiwan"],", including mpox."]},{"k":"p","s":["There has been a significant increase in cases of dengue fever in the south of Taiwan (including the cities of Kaohsiung and Tainan). Take precautions to avoid mosquito bites. See ",["key updates from the Taiwan Centers for Disease Control","https://www.cdc.gov.tw/En"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Taiwan. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re bringing any prescribed medicine into Taiwan, bring the prescription issued by your doctor, hospital or clinic that shows the medicine is for your personal use. The amount of medication you bring must be consistent with the amount stated on the prescription. You cannot bring cannabis oil or cannabis-derived medication into Taiwan, even if it’s legally prescribed elsewhere."]},{"k":"p","s":["For further information on the legal status of a specific medicine, contact the Taipei Representative Office in London."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Taiwan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Taiwan’s health and dental facilities offer a range of routine, emergency and outpatient services. Some have English-speaking staff. Hospitals operate on a ’pay as you use’ basis. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment in Taiwan including possible repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical providers in Taiwan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/taiwan-list-of-medical-practitioners-hospitals"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Taiwan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance and fire: 119"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 110"]},{"k":"p","s":["Coastguard: 118"]},{"k":"p","s":["Domestic abuse and sexual assault hotline: 113"]},{"k":"p","s":["Any further assistance: 0800 024 111 (‘Information for Foreigners in Taiwan’ helpline)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Taiwan"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Taiwan"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Taiwan"]," in Taiwan."]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Taiwan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/taiwan-bereavement-death-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Taiwan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/taiwan-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/taiwan/british-office-taipei"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/taiwan/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Taiwan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-taiwan"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":15429,"change":"Updated information of the health risks you’ll face in Taiwan (‘Health’ page)."}};
